const faq = [
  { q: 'What is the Viking raven banner called?', a: 'The Old Norse name is Hrafnsmerki ("raven mark" or "raven standard"). The word merki means a mark, sign, or standard. The banner is also called Hrafnfáni ("raven banner") in some sources.' },
  { q: 'Who carried the Viking raven banner?', a: 'The raven banner is associated primarily with Scandinavian and Norse-descended rulers and their armies. The most historically documented instances involve the Danish Vikings (at the Battle of Ashdown, 871 CE, in the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle) and the Earls of Orkney (attested in Orkneyinga Saga).' },
